From b5ae2ca4c874ce57e7442237b68e45f149d26a90 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: shota <monyuonyu@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 10:42:38 +0900
Subject: [PATCH 081/122] TABLE: the table content for R2010+ from earlier
 versions

Since R2010 the TABLE entity has the table content (20.4.97) instead of
the cells of R2000-R2007 (20.4.96.1), which we did not convert: the 13
tables of the R14-R2007 drawings had no rows, columns and cells as
R2010+, and the horizontal direction was 0.

* src/encode.c (upconvert_TABLE): New, the reverse of
downconvert_TABLE: columns, rows, one content per cell (the text, the
R2007 value, the FIELD or the block with its attribute values), the
alignment, color and text height overrides, the merged ranges, the
horizontal direction and one break row range.
(table_strdup): New.
* src/encode.h: Declare upconvert_TABLE.
* src/dwg2.spec (TABLE): Call it for R2010+ from earlier versions.
* src/free.c (free_TABLE_r2000): New, free its allocations.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/dwg2.spec |   4 +
 src/encode.c  | 212 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 src/encode.h  |   1 +
 src/free.c    |  50 ++++++++++++
 4 files changed, 267 insertions(+)

